          "type": "User",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/KageBinary"
        },
        "body": "One more, non-blocking but worth folding in: routing thrown text through `appendChunk` means it is dropped outright once the cap has fired, because `appendChunk` starts with `if (run.truncated) return;`. A command that floods and *then* throws reaches the client as only `output exceeded N bytes and was truncated` — no reason. main appended it unconditionally, so it's a regression in the case where the diagnostic matters most.\n\nFix + test: **Hiro-Chiba/Ix#4**. Your existing cap test is unaffected and passes unchanged.",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/ix-infrastructure/Ix/pull/436#issuecomment-5296782368",
        "api_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/ix-infrastructure/Ix/issues/comments/5296782368",
        "created_at": "2026-08-14T18:26:00Z",
